<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 4th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 300s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/4th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 350 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10835 5703" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 350 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="5304" cy="942" r="184"/><text x="5304" y="1019" font-size="221">1</text></g><g><circle cx="6357" cy="1235" r="184"/><text x="6357" y="1313" font-size="221">2</text></g><g><circle cx="5772" cy="1297" r="184"/><text x="5772" y="1374" font-size="221">3</text></g><g><circle cx="2331" cy="1704" r="184"/><text x="2331" y="1782" font-size="221">4</text></g><g><circle cx="7362" cy="1550" r="184"/><text x="7362" y="1627" font-size="221">5</text></g><g><circle cx="6060" cy="1908" r="184"/><text x="6060" y="1985" font-size="221">6</text></g><g><circle cx="8115" cy="1035" r="184"/><text x="8115" y="1112" font-size="221">7</text></g><g><circle cx="4821" cy="1043" r="184"/><text x="4821" y="1120" font-size="221">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 350 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Roman Egypt &middot; Goguryeo &middot; Aksumite Empire &middot; Teotihuacan &middot; Gupta Empire &middot; Lusitania &middot; Sasanian Empire &middot; Roman Empire</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Edict of Milan</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Adrianople</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Fei River</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>First Council of Nicaea</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Canhe Slope</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Solicinium</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Constantine I</li><li>Ammianus Marcellinus</li><li>Samudragupta</li><li>Licinius</li><li>Jerome</li><li>Shapur II</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>309–379 CE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 272–337 CE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 335–375 CE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 347–420</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 330–c. 400</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 265–325</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 300s, 50 recorded states were founded and 54 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Roman Empire, the Sasanian Empire and the Roman Egypt. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 4th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/4th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 4th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Roman Empire <span>27 BCE – 476 CE</span></li><li>Sasanian Empire <span>224 CE – 651 CE</span></li><li>Roman Egypt <span>30 BCE – 641 CE</span></li><li>Teotihuacan <span>100 BCE – 550 CE</span></li><li>Gupta Empire <span>240 CE – 550 CE</span></li><li>Aksumite Empire <span>100 CE – 940 CE</span></li><li>Goguryeo <span>37 BCE – 668 CE</span></li><li>Lusitania <span>27 BCE – 439 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Edict of Milan <span>313 CE</span></li><li>First Council of Nicaea <span>325</span></li><li>Battle of Solicinium <span>368</span></li><li>Battle of Adrianople <span>378 CE</span></li><li>Battle of Fei River <span>383</span></li><li>Battle of Canhe Slope <span>395</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Constantine I <span>2: c. 272–337 CE</span></li><li>Ammianus Marcellinus <span>5: c. 330–c. 400</span></li><li>Samudragupta <span>3: c. 335–375 CE</span></li><li>Licinius <span>6: c. 265–325</span></li><li>Jerome <span>4: c. 347–420</span></li><li>Shapur II <span>1: 309–379 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
